            <ArticleTitle>Mental practice for chronic pain in people with spinal cord injury: a systematic review protocol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2004-2012</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11124/JBISRIR-2016-003149</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="REVIEW QUESTION/OBJECTIVE:" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">The primary objective of this systematic review is to identify the effects of mental practice (MP) interventions on chronic neuropathic and nociceptive pain and motor function recovery in individuals after spinal cord injury (SCI). Where possible, this review will also describe the optimal type and dosage (i.e. frequency, intensity and duration) of MP interventions for patients with SCI.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
